{parent=ii}

Applying the <Euclidean algorithm>,
$$
\begin{aligned}
3211&=2508+703,\\
2508&=3(703)+399,\\
703&=399+304,\\
399&=304+95,\\
304&=3(95)+19,\\
95&=5(19).
\end{aligned}
$$
Hence $\gcd(2508,3211)=19$. Since $19$ does not divide $55$, the <linear Diophantine equation solvability criterion> gives
$$
\boxed{2508x+3211y=55\text{ has no integer solution}.}
$$

